course: dictionary
lesson: 7932
title: Realistic: real or make-believe?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Realistic comes from real. It has two meanings. First, it means sensible about what can really happen: «a realistic plan» is one you can actually carry out. Second, it means looking very like the real thing: «a realistic painting of a horse» looks like a horse you might see in a field.
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. «The Owl and the Pussy-cat went to sea» is not realistic at all, because a cat and an owl do not sail away in a boat. It is fun. Ask yourself: could this really happen, or is it only make-believe?
explain: In maths, a realistic answer makes sense. A person cannot be 5 metres tall, so that answer is not realistic. In stories, realistic fiction tells about things that could really happen.
fact: Realistic means like real life, or sensible about what can really happen.
fact: Useful phrases: be realistic, realistic goal, realistic fiction, look realistic.
fact: A realistic goal is one you can actually reach.
fact: «A PEGI 7 game may have only mild, cartoon-style fighting, like soft cartoon monsters.» Cartoon monsters are not realistic, but PEGI 16 and 18 games can have realistic violence, which looks like real life.
fact: Words such as realistic help us judge plans, pictures and stories by asking whether they could really happen.
exercise: «The Owl and the Pussy-cat went to sea» is not realistic at all. What does that tell you? | It is a realistic painting of the sea | It is a sensible plan for a holiday | It is a true story about a boat trip | *It could not really happen; it is make-believe for fun
exercise: A painting that looks just like a real horse is called what? | Cartoon | Silly | Invisible | *Realistic
exercise: Mia wants a goal. Which one is a realistic goal? | Fly over the school to the moon | *Walk 1 km this week, then add a little more each week | Run a marathon next week with no training | Win every race in the world by Friday
test: «A PEGI 7 game may have only mild, cartoon-style fighting.» Why is this not realistic violence? | Cartoon-style fighting is very scary | Realistic violence is always funny | *Cartoon-style fighting does not look like real life | Mild means it lasts for a very long time
test: In maths, a child who says they are 5 metres tall has given what kind of answer? | A realistic goal | *Not a realistic answer | A realistic painting | A realistic answer
exam: Which sentence uses realistic to mean sensible about what can really happen? | *«Saving a little money each week is a realistic plan.» | «The dragon ate the moon for its lunch, which was realistic.» | «Her goal was to fly to the sun by Friday, a realistic target.»
